Does the bring-up plan act on what QA found? Do not judge whether the board is
right: a plan for a faulty board passes if it targets the fault.

Polarity checks:
{{ ref('polarity') | select('mapping') | list | tojson(indent=2) }}

Bring-up plan:
{{ ref('bringup') | tojson(indent=2) }}

Fail if any of these hold:
- a polarised part has no unpowered inspection in "pre_power"
- a part whose polarity check found an issue is inspected only generically,
  without naming the issue
- the first powered check confirms the happy path instead of forcing the
  failure condition (block the beam, remove the signal, disconnect a wire) and
  expecting the board to report it. A sensor that only ever reports success
  cannot be told from one that always says "clear".
Reply with only valid JSON: {"results": "pass"} or {"results": "fail"}.
